% M7-T6 / D-0070: A CORRECT ANSWER WHOSE PROOF THE CHECKER REJECTED. FIXED; this model
% is an ordinary passing model test and its proof is verified on every run. What follows
% is the shape it was reduced to, kept because it is the regression.
%
% Nine variables, five constraints, NO global constraint. The solver answers
% xs = [1,1,9,1,1,1,2,1,1], which satisfies every constraint by inspection
% (x3=1 != x6=2; x6=2 != x7=1; -2(1)+9-1+1 = 7). veripb 3.0.2 then rejects the
% proof at the level-0 backtrack nogood on line 48:
%
%   The constraint is not implied by reverse unit propagation (RUP) from core
%   and derived database.
%
% Found by M7-T3 while measuring the MiniZinc library, and shown PRE-EXISTING
% rather than caused by keeping a global native: the same 2001 fuzz seeds gave 3
% RUP failures with all_different native and 5 with it decomposed to pairwise
% int_ne -- overlapping but not identical sets, so the defect is upstream of the
% global entirely. This reproducer has no global at all, which is why it is the
% one to debug.
%
% This is M1-T44's shape: the answer is right, every step looks valid, and the artefact
% is the thing that is wrong. THE CAUSE (D-0070): the level-6 decision `x7 >= 2` settled
% past the hole int_ne(x6,x7) punches at x7 = 2 and landed on x7 >= 3. Search.bridges
% writes that settle down as a line conditioned on every ancestor decision, but the
% implication graph has no edge for a settle, so Learn.levels never names those
% ancestors' levels and the nogood filtered by Learn.levels dropped them -- leaving the
% nogood no longer entailing its own bridge. Fixed in lib/core/search.ml; the break lane
% is test/unit/test_learn.ml's [test_settle_bridge_survives_the_filter].
var 1..11: x0;
var 1..11: x1;
var 1..11: x2;
var 1..11: x3;
var 1..11: x4;
var 1..11: x5;
var 1..11: x6;
var 1..11: x7;
var 1..11: x8;
var bool: b0;
var bool: b1;
var bool: b2;
var 0..11: y0;
var 0..11: y1;
array [1..9] of var int: xs:: output_array([1..9]) = [x0,x1,x2,x3,x4,x5,x6,x7,x8];
constraint int_ne(x3,x6);
constraint int_ne(x6,x7);
constraint int_lin_eq([-2,1,-1,1],[x7,x2,x8,x0],7);
constraint int_lin_le_reif([-2,-2],[x3,x6],-9,b0);
constraint int_lin_le_reif([2,1,-1,-1],[x7,x1,x0,x2],6,b1);
solve satisfy;
